{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310522,"nonce":"b+k7sFnG1r/LBwNt/zDe3sGi+t0=","title":"nue/nue/arch/LlamaModel.hx:65 `var hIn = h.clone(); h = block.forward(hIn);` cannot drop to bare `h = block.forward(h)` even after ...","message":"After commit da4614c made `TransformerBlock.forward` effectively in-place (residuals via `addInto`), the audit predicted the defensive clone at [nue/nue/arch/LlamaModel.hx:65](nue/nue/arch/LlamaModel.hx#L65) could drop:\n\n```haxe\n// Current (defensive):\nvar hIn = h.clone();\nh = block.forward(hIn);\n\n// Predicted (after addInto):\nh = block.forward(h);\n```\n\n**Why it failed:** the bare rebind form SIGSEGVs at exit 139 during generation. The buffer that `block.forward(h)` returns is the same buffer that the in-place addInto mutated, but the IR scope cleanup / drop analyzer tears it down between the call return and the reassign on the rebinding shape `h = call(h)`. This is the same shape class as [[bugs-clone-view-passthrough-invariant]] in that it depends on subtle interactions between drop analysis and the new strict-`@:move` enforcement.\n\n**Why this matters:** the LlamaModel `forwardIds` block loop runs 16 times per token. Each defensive clone is a `[seq, hidden=2048]` F32 alloc + memcpy + free — ~64 KB per clone × 16 layers × tokens. The audit estimated ~3 MB allocator-churn savings per 24-token decode if this single clone dropped. Leaving it unrealized means commit da4614c is **mostly architecture-hygiene at present hot loops** — the residual addInto sites land cleanly, but the dependent clone drop does not.\n\n**How to apply:** when proposing fix-forward for the drop analyzer / IR scope cleanup, this is the **highest-leverage single-call-site test case**. Once fixed, recheck whether the LlamaModel rebind drops; expect ~3 MB allocator churn off the 24-token bench and possibly a small wall-clock measurable depending on allocator pressure.\n\n**Repro**:\n1. Edit `nue/nue/arch/LlamaModel.hx:65` to bare `h = block.forward(h);`\n2. Rebuild: `cargo build --release --bin rayzor`\n3. Run llama-chat: SIGSEGV / exit 139 mid-generation\n4. Document occurs in stack trace.\n\nThe inline `Note:` block at LlamaModel.hx:64 documents the constraint at the source level so future maintainers don't accidentally hit the trap.\n\n**Hypothesised root cause** (un-verified): the drop analyzer pre-computes the drop schedule before the call-return value's lifetime is established; when the lvalue is the same as the call's rvalue argument, the pre-call drop fires on what will become the new binding's storage. Investigation path: instrument `compiler/src/ir/drop_analysis.rs` to log every (binding, drop-site, called-fn) tuple around an aliased rebind; compare against the non-aliased clone case to identify the divergence point.\n\nRelated: [[project-addinto-fused-kernel]], [[project-move-clone-enforced]], [[bugs-clone-view-passthrough-invariant]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_addinto_rebind_clone_drop_failure` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}